<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 20px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0; font-size: 2em;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.2em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 4th Grade (CEFR: A1.2)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Our Traditional Style of Dress</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> She Is Wearing a Pollera.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: productive: Write simple sentences on familiar topics. interactive: Edit classmates' written work.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write simple descriptions about traditional clothing (e.g., 'The pollera is beautiful.'). Can edit, for clarity, classmates' sentences about traditional dress (e.g., add 'colorful' to describe the dress). Can revise, for detail, written descriptions of traditional clothing (e.g., add 'worn' at festivals to describe the dress).</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center; margin-top: 30px;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays pictures of different traditional Panamanian clothing (e.g., pollera, montuno) on the board. Students orally identify them and shout out one word to describe each (e.g., "beautiful," "colorful," "festive"). The teacher quickly writes these words on the board. Then, the teacher shows a picture of a woman wearing a pollera and asks, "What is she wearing?" to elicit "She is wearing a pollera."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher writes two simple sentences on the board describing the displayed pollera, for example: "The pollera is beautiful. It has many colors." The teacher reads the sentences aloud, modeling clear pronunciation, especially of /w/ in 'wearing' and /t/ in 'traditional'. The teacher points to the words as they read, demonstrating how written words represent spoken language. The teacher also blends the sounds of 'dress' (/dr/ /ɛs/) and 'pretty' (/pr-ɪ-t-i/) orally, then writes the words and asks students to repeat.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is the pollera ugly or beautiful?" (Expected answer: Beautiful.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Does the pollera have few colors or many colors?" (Expected answer: Many colors.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When do women wear the pollera?" (Expected answer: At festivals/celebrations.)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Our Traditional Style of Dress"</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short, illustrated descriptive paragraph about traditional Panamanian attire. The text introduces new vocabulary and grammar in context, focusing on simple sentences. For example: "This is a pollera. It is traditional clothing. Women wear it for celebrations. It is beautiful and festive. Some polleras have gold jewelry. They represent our community. She is wearing a pollera now."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Understands and uses simple written descriptions of familiar cultural items.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist questions:</b> "What is the text about?" (Expected: A pollera/traditional dress.) "Is it about food or clothes?" (Expected: Clothes.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Students read sentences based on the text and write "T" or "F." For example: "The pollera is modern." (F) "Women wear polleras for events." (T) "The pollera is cultural attire." (T)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Matching:</b> Match words from the text (e.g., 'celebration', 'jewelry', 'represent', 'festive') with simple pictures or definitions.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10-12 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Writing</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Writing simple sentences using present continuous ('She is wearing...'), present simple ('Women wear...'), and target vocabulary (attire, beautiful, festive, cultural, represent, community, explain).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice: Sentence Scramble & Completion (Writing):</b> The teacher writes scrambled sentences about traditional clothing on the board or provides a worksheet. Students unscramble the words to form correct sentences. Example: "pollera / a / is / She / wearing." (She is wearing a pollera.) Then, students complete sentences with missing vocabulary words from a word bank (e.g., 'festive', 'traditional', 'beautiful', 'wear'). Example: "The pollera is very _____. Women ______ it at celebrations." (beautiful, wear).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice: Guided Sentence Writing (Writing):</b> Students receive sentence frames and pictures of different traditional Panamanian clothing (e.g., pollera, tembleques, montuno). For each picture, they complete sentences using the present continuous and present simple, incorporating target adjectives and nouns. Example frames: "She is wearing a _____. It is _____ and _____. People wear it for _____ events." (Students write: "She is wearing a pollera. It is beautiful and cultural. People wear it for festive events.") The teacher encourages the use of words like 'attire', 'jewelry', 'showcase'.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Check and Peer Editing (Interactive Writing):</b> In pairs, students exchange their completed sentences from activity 2. They read each other's sentences and use a simple checklist to check for: 1) correct vocabulary usage, 2) complete sentences, and 3) good description (e.g., "Is it clear? Can you add a descriptive word like 'colorful' or 'pretty'?"). They politely suggest one correction or addition to their partner's work. This directly addresses the "Edit classmates' written work" objective.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">15-18 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Our Traditional Style of Dress"</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task format:</b> Individual Written Product – Descriptive Paragraph.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Task Description:</b> Students choose one traditional Panamanian clothing item (e.g., pollera, montuno, tembleques) from a selection of pictures provided by the teacher, or one they know. They then write a short descriptive paragraph (3-5 simple sentences) about their chosen attire. They must use at least two sentences with the present continuous or present simple, and at least three of the target vocabulary words (e.g., 'attire', 'beautiful', 'festive', 'celebration', 'represent', 'community', 'jewelry'). A simple sentence starter could be provided: "This is a _____. It is _____." This task allows students to apply the learned grammar and vocabulary to describe traditional clothing, fulfilling the "Write simple sentences on familiar topics" objective.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Writing simple, clear sentences; descriptive detail; correct use of target grammar and vocabulary; completing the writing task.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10-12 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> The written descriptive paragraphs from Stage 4 will be collected for formative assessment. Additionally, students will engage in a final peer editing session where they revise their own work based on partner feedback and then provide one written suggestion for another classmate's paragraph (e.g., "Add 'colorful' to describe the dress.").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Observation/Rubric):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity of sentences and ideas (Can write simple descriptions).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct use of present simple and present continuous.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of target vocabulary (e.g., 'attire', 'celebration', 'beautiful', 'represent', 'wear').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Effort in editing classmates' work (e.g., providing relevant suggestions for clarity or detail).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete a quick exit ticket with two prompts:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I can write _____ sentences about traditional clothing." (e.g., 3, 4, many)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One new word I used today is _____."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of writing about traditional clothes was easy for me today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of writing was difficult, and what can I do next time to make it easier?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> The teacher considers: "Did students successfully write simple sentences describing traditional clothing? Was the peer editing effective in improving clarity and detail? What adjustments are needed for sentence complexity or vocabulary support in future writing tasks? Were the specific grammatical structures adequately applied? How can I ensure more students revise their work for detail as mentioned in the learning outcome?"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> The written descriptions from this lesson can be used in Lesson 5 (Mediation & Integration) as a basis for students to explain their chosen attire to a classmate who might not be familiar with it, or to include in a small class project showcasing traditional dress.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">3-5 min</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>